### Command names and descriptions (shown on the toolbar, File menu, command search and right-click menus)
### The ID is the command ID with "." and "_" turned into "-", prefixed by action-. Descriptions add -tip.

## Animation

action-anim-appearance = Appearance
action-anim-appearance-tip = Add a step that changes the selected part's appearance over the step's length (the design's appearance is unchanged). Pick the appearance again on the step bar
action-anim-auto-explode-all = Auto Explode: All Levels
action-anim-auto-explode-all-tip = Move parts away from the assembly center automatically, and parts inside parts away from that part's center. Choose one step or sequential, trail lines and explode scale, then OK
action-anim-auto-explode-one = Auto Explode: One Level
action-anim-auto-explode-one-tip = Move parts away from the assembly center automatically (direct children only; parts inside are not moved). Choose one step (all at once) or sequential (1 second per part), trail lines and explode scale, then OK
action-anim-drive = Joint Motion
action-anim-drive-tip = Add a step that drives a joint from its lower to its upper limit (without limits: 90 deg for revolute, the part's length for slider). Edit the values and length on the step bar
action-anim-explode = Explode Move
action-anim-explode-tip = Add a step that moves parts by a direction and distance at the end of the step bar: part face → direction arrow → distance. The design's shape is unchanged
action-anim-view = View
action-anim-view-tip = Add a step that moves to the current viewpoint at the end of the step bar (from the previous view step's viewpoint). Turn on "Record" on the step bar to add one each time you finish moving the view
action-anim-visibility = Show/Hide
action-anim-visibility-tip = Add a step at the end of the step bar that hides the selected parts at the step's start (or shows them if hidden). Select parts first, or press and then click a face

## Assembly

action-asm-bom = Bill of Materials
action-asm-bom-tip = Table of count, material, size (length × width × thickness), volume and mass per part. Pick the columns with "Columns" on the table. Parts with the same size and material are counted together
action-asm-bom-csv = Export Bill of Materials…
action-asm-bom-csv-tip = Export the bill of materials as CSV (opens in spreadsheet software)
action-asm-contact-reach = Value Until Contact
action-asm-contact-reach-tip = Drive a joint from its current value to a target and report at which value it hits a partner in a contact set, and how much further it can move (the shape is unchanged)
action-asm-contacts = Enable Contact Sets
action-asm-contacts-tip = Toggle whether dragging a joint's part stops at partners in contact sets (each set can also be toggled with the eye of "Contact Sets" in the browser)
action-asm-fastener = Standard Parts
action-asm-fastener-tip = Insert screws, nuts, washers or ball bearings into holes: hole's top face → hole's top circles (any number) → Enter. The size is picked from the hole diameter; type and length can be changed later. Counts appear in the bill of materials
action-asm-place-occurrence = Place Another Instance
action-asm-place-occurrence-tip = Place the selected component once more without copying its shape (an occurrence). Editing the original changes every occurrence, and the bill of materials counts them as the same part. Use Make Independent to cut an occurrence loose from the original
action-asm-occurrence-detach = Make Independent
action-asm-occurrence-detach-tip = Turn the occurrence into an ordinary component holding a copy of its current shape. Later edits to the original no longer change it
action-asm-occurrence-sync = Match Original
action-asm-occurrence-sync-tip = Add bodies that were later added to the original component to this occurrence, placed the same way
action-asm-interference = Interference
action-asm-interference-tip = Check visible bodies for overlaps, list the volume per pair in a table and show the overlaps in red in 3D (at the positions joints have moved them to). "Include coincident faces" also lists pairs that only touch at a face
action-asm-joint = As-built Joint
action-asm-joint-tip = Join parts where they are now: face of the moving part → axis (circle or edge) → face of the base part. It can be moved by value
action-asm-joints = Joint List
action-asm-joints-tip = Table of each joint's type, moving part, base, bodies that move with it, axis and current value (also used by AI to read the assembly)
action-asm-link-insert = Insert Link…
action-asm-link-insert-tip = Insert a part from another file while keeping it linked to the source. When the source changes a mark appears; update it from the part's right-click menu
action-asm-link-relink = Choose Source File Again…
action-asm-link-relink-tip = Pick a source file that was moved or replaced to replace the copy. Bodies with the same names follow; bodies not found are reported (can be undone)
action-asm-motion-link = Motion Link
action-asm-motion-link-tip = Link the motion of two joints by a ratio (e.g. the handle turns 360 deg and the jaw moves 10 mm). The later joint in the timeline follows the earlier one; edit the ratio and direction on the later joint
action-asm-motion-study = Motion Study
action-asm-motion-study-tip = Move several joints together by setting their values with keys on a 0–100 step bar to check how the mechanism moves. Shapes and values are unchanged. The study is kept in the document
action-asm-move-part = Move Part
action-asm-move-part-tip = Move the selected part with its bodies by value (adds a position feature). Pressing M with a part selected also starts it
action-asm-new-component = New Component
action-asm-new-component-tip = Make the selected bodies into a component (an empty component if nothing is selected). It appears in the browser's component tree; rename it with "Rename" on the right-click menu
action-asm-new-constraint = Constraint
action-asm-new-constraint-tip = Move part 1 so that its face meets a face of part 2: click a face of part 1, Ctrl+click a face of part 2, then press. Add rows (pairs of faces) to satisfy them all at once
action-asm-new-contact-set = New Contact Set
action-asm-new-contact-set-tip = Make the selected bodies (two or more) a contact set. While contact sets are enabled, dragging a joint's part stops just before it digs into a partner in the same set
action-asm-new-rigid-group = Rigid Group
action-asm-new-rigid-group-tip = Make the selected components (two or more) one block. Whichever part a joint or drag moves, they all move together
action-asm-snap-joint = Joint
action-asm-snap-joint-tip = Move part 1 to meet part 2 and join them: face of part 1 → origin → face of part 2 → origin. Type, angle and offset can be changed later

## Design

action-cad-add-datum-axis = Construction Axis
action-cad-add-datum-axis-tip = Create a straight line to use as an axis for revolves and patterns. Select an edge for an axis along it, a cylindrical face for its axis, two corners for an axis through them, or two flat faces for their intersection
action-cad-add-datum-plane = Construction Plane
action-cad-add-datum-plane-tip = Create a plane to use as a reference for sketches and features. Select a face or plane for an offset plane, two flat faces for a midplane, or three corners for a plane through them
action-cad-add-datum-point = Construction Point
action-cad-add-datum-point-tip = Create a point to use as a reference for construction planes and axes. Select a corner for the corner, a circular edge for its center, or nothing for a point by coordinates
action-cad-add-sketch = Create Sketch
action-cad-add-sketch-tip = Add an empty sketch. On the flat face selected in the 3D view, or, if none, press and then click the XY, YZ or ZX plane
action-cad-add-sketch3d = Add 3D Sketch
action-cad-add-sketch3d-tip = Add a sketch whose points and lines are placed in 3D. Draw shapes at different heights or at right angles in one sketch, and define them with along-axis, parallel, perpendicular and 3D angle constraints. A selected flat face becomes the reference
action-cad-canvas-calibrate = Calibrate
action-cad-canvas-calibrate-tip = Click two points on the image whose distance is known and type the real distance to scale the image
action-cad-canvas-insert = Canvas…
action-cad-canvas-insert-tip = Place a photo or drawing as an image to trace with sketches. It goes on the selected flat face, otherwise on the origin plane facing the current view
action-cad-canvas-plane = Select Plane
action-cad-canvas-plane-tip = Set the plane for the canvas by clicking the square of the origin XY, YZ or ZX plane, or a flat face of a body
action-cad-chamfer = Chamfer
action-cad-chamfer-tip = Press, then click an edge or face to apply it and go on to the value fields (a face means all edges around it; Ctrl+click to pick several). If edges or faces are already selected, it applies to them
action-cad-draft-plane = Select Pull Direction
action-cad-draft-plane-tip = Set the pull-direction plane of the selected draft by clicking the square of the origin XY, YZ or ZX plane, a construction plane, or a flat face of a body
action-cad-extrude = Extrude
action-cad-extrude-tip = Press, then click the profiles or a flat face of a body to extrude (overlapping shapes can be picked by region; Ctrl+click to pick several). Set the height with the mouse or a number and press Enter. While setting the height, hover another flat face to extend up to it; clicking then creates the extrude with the extent set to that object. With a flat face of a body selected first, that face is extruded. A sketch of open lines is extruded as a 2 mm thick wall (thin extrude)
action-cad-extrude-regions = Reselect Profiles
action-cad-extrude-regions-tip = Add or remove profiles of the selected extrude by clicking (starts with the current profiles selected). Press Enter to confirm
action-cad-extrude-to-face = Up to Face
action-cad-extrude-to-face-tip = Extrude the selected extrude up to the clicked flat face, vertex or construction plane (an inclined face trims the end of the tool body). It cuts if the extrusion passes through the body, and joins if it does not
action-cad-fillet = Fillet
action-cad-fillet-tip = Press, then click an edge or face to apply it and go on to the value fields (a face means all edges around it; Ctrl+click to pick several). If edges or faces are already selected, it applies to them
action-cad-hole-add = Add Same Hole
action-cad-hole-add-tip = Add the same hole as the selected one on the same face where you click. Press Enter to finish
action-cad-hole-on-face = Hole
action-cad-hole-on-face-tip = Press, then click a flat face → the hole center → the diameter to make a hole. Click more centers to add the same hole. Edit depth, counterbore or countersink and thread in the fields, then OK or Enter. Esc cancels
action-cad-hole-to-face = Select Hole Stop Face
action-cad-hole-to-face-tip = Make the selected hole go down to the clicked flat face (on an inclined face the bottom follows it) or vertex
action-cad-import-step = Import STEP…
action-cad-import-step-tip = Import a part made in another CAD program. Add holes and pockets to it and use it for machining and measuring
action-cad-loft = Loft
action-cad-loft-tip = Press, then click the sections (profiles drawn on different planes) in the order to join them, and pick guide rail lines (or press Enter if none)
action-cad-loft-point = Reselect End Point
action-cad-measure = Measure Volume
action-cad-measure-tip = Volume, surface area and bounding box of the selected body (or the last body)
action-cad-mirror-on-face = Mirror on This Face
action-cad-mirror-on-face-tip = Copy the last extrude or other shape to the other side of this face
action-cad-mirror-plane = Select Mirror Plane
action-cad-mirror-plane-tip = Set the mirror plane of the selected mirror by clicking the square of the origin XY, YZ or ZX plane, a construction plane, or a flat face of a body
action-cad-move-axis = Select Rotation Axis
action-cad-move-axis-tip = Set the rotation axis of the selected move/copy by clicking the origin X, Y or Z axis, a sketch line or a body edge (a circular edge gives its axis)
action-cad-pattern-split-copies = Split Copies into Bodies
action-cad-pattern-split-copies-tip = Make each copy of the selected body pattern or mirror (with "Copies as separate bodies" on) a separate body. Use it again after raising the count to split the new copies too
action-cad-revolve = Revolve
action-cad-revolve-tip = Select a planar face first, or press and click sketch regions (Ctrl+click to pick several), click an axis in the same plane, and set the angle with the mouse or a number (Enter alone makes a full turn)
action-cad-revolve-axis = Select Revolve Axis
action-cad-revolve-axis-tip = Set the axis of the selected revolve by clicking the origin X, Y or Z axis in the profile's plane, or a sketch line (construction lines of the profile's sketch too)
action-cad-revolve-regions = Reselect Profiles
action-cad-revolve-regions-tip = Add or remove profiles of the selected revolve by clicking (starts with the current profiles selected). Press Enter to confirm
action-cad-revolve-to-face = Select Revolve Stop Face
action-cad-revolve-to-face-tip = Revolve the selected revolve up to the clicked flat face (a face containing the revolve axis)
action-cad-sketch-auto-constrain = AutoConstrain
action-cad-sketch-auto-constrain-tip = Add the coincident, horizontal, vertical, tangent and other constraints and dimensions that already hold at the current positions of the selected sketch, only where missing (equal is not guessed)
action-cad-sketch-export-dxf = Save as DXF…
action-cad-sketch-export-dxf-tip = Export the lines of the selected sketch (except construction lines) to DXF
action-cad-sketch-export-svg = Save as SVG…
action-cad-sketch-export-svg-tip = Export the lines of the selected sketch (except construction lines) to SVG at 1 mm = 1 unit; join connected lines into closed outlines
action-cad-sketch-find = Find Sketch Entities
action-cad-sketch-find-tip = List the points, lines, circles and so on of the selected sketch in a table, filtered by type, construction, how constrained, length, radius and region
action-cad-sketch-insert-dxf = Insert DXF…
action-cad-sketch-insert-dxf-tip = Add the lines, arcs, circles and points of a DXF to the selected sketch. Without a selected sketch, a new one is made on the XY plane
action-cad-sketch-insert-svg = Insert SVG…
action-cad-sketch-insert-svg-tip = Add the lines and curves of an SVG to the selected sketch (curves become line segments and arcs). Without a selected sketch, a new one is made on the XY plane
action-cad-sketch-redefine-plane = Redefine Sketch Plane
action-cad-sketch-redefine-plane-tip = Move the selected sketch to the clicked face or the XY, YZ or ZX plane (lines and constraints are kept)
action-cad-sketch-on-face = Sketch on Face
action-cad-sketch-on-face-tip = Select a flat face in the 3D view, then press
action-cad-split-plane = Select Splitting Plane
action-cad-split-plane-tip = Set the plane of the selected split body by clicking the square of the origin XY, YZ or ZX plane, a construction plane, or a flat face of a body
action-cad-sweep = Sweep
action-cad-sweep-tip = Press, then click the profiles to move and click the sketch line to use as the path. One end of the path must lie on the profile's plane
action-cad-text-explode = Explode Text into Lines
action-cad-text-explode-tip = Turn the selected text into line segments of a new sketch on the same plane (each can be moved and edited). The original text is suppressed (not deleted)
action-cad-text-font = Change Font
action-cad-text-font-tip = Use an outline font on this PC (TrueType, OpenType) for the selected text. The glyphs used are stored in the document, so the shape stays the same on a PC without the font
action-cad-text-at-point = Text at Sketch Point
action-cad-text-at-point-tip = Place text centered on a lone sketch point. The point can be moved with constraints
action-cad-text-on-face = Text on Face
action-cad-text-on-face-tip = Select a flat face, then press to place single-line font text at the face's center. Trace it with engraving, or cut or raise it with an extrude
action-cad-text-on-path = Text on Sketch Line
action-cad-text-on-path-tip = Lay text along the first line of the sketch (construction lines too). On a circle it starts at the top, facing out
action-cad-thread = Thread
action-cad-thread-tip = Press, then click a cylindrical face (outside of a boss or inside of a hole) to fill in the thread size and pitch nearest the face's diameter. Edit size, length and direction in the fields, then OK or Enter
action-cad-timeline-read-latest-bodies = Read Latest Bodies Everywhere
action-cad-timeline-read-latest-bodies-tip = Make every feature that still reads a body as it was when picked (the older reading) read the latest shape instead (one undo step)
action-cad-timeline-read-latest-body = Read Latest Body
action-cad-timeline-read-latest-body-tip = Make a feature that reads a body as it was when picked (the older reading) read the shape with the features added later (can be undone)
action-cad-timeline-roll-back = Rollback Position
action-cad-timeline-roll-back-tip = Move the timeline marker to leave the features after it out of the calculation (can be undone)
action-cad-visibility = Show/Hide
action-cad-visibility-tip = Open or close the eye of a body, sketch, construction plane, component, group or origin (saved in the document and can be undone; shapes are not recalculated)

## Manufacture

action-cam-add-adaptive = Adaptive Clearing
action-cam-add-adaptive-tip = Select bottom faces (several allowed) or a sketch with closed profiles, then press. Keeps the tool's engagement constant so each pass can go deeper and cut faster
action-cam-add-chamfer = Chamfer
action-cam-add-chamfer-tip = Bevel edges with a V-bit. Selected faces give their edges; with nothing selected, the edges of the highest face
action-cam-add-circular = Bore/Circular
action-cam-add-circular-tip = Cut round holes and bosses reachable from above in a helix from a circle along the wall. Selected hole or boss walls give those; with nothing selected, all of them
action-cam-add-contour = Contour
action-cam-add-contour-tip = Cut the outline of the selected faces, or the part's outline if none are selected
action-cam-add-drill = Drilling
action-cam-add-drill-tip = Add to the last setup
action-cam-add-engrave = Engrave
action-cam-add-engrave-tip = Trace the sketch's lines at a set depth. A selected sketch gives its lines; with nothing selected, the last sketch
action-cam-add-face = Face
action-cam-add-face-tip = Add to the last setup
action-cam-add-flat3d = Flat (3D)
action-cam-add-flat3d-tip = Find upward flat faces and finish them at their heights. Selected faces limit it to those
action-cam-add-laser = Laser
action-cam-add-laser-tip = Trace sketch lines with a laser or fill closed shapes. Needs a laser tool in the tool library. A selected sketch gives its lines; with nothing selected, the last sketch
action-cam-add-manual-nc = Manual NC
action-cam-add-manual-nc-tip = Stop between operations (to move clamps or clear chips). With an operation selected, it goes after it. Before stopping the spindle is stopped and retracted; after resuming it spins up again and waits
action-cam-add-morph3d = Morphed Spiral (3D)
action-cam-add-morph3d-tip = Finish gentle surfaces without lifting, with one spiral that shrinks to follow the shape of the machining boundary. Without a boundary, the part's outline (uses a ball end mill if there is one)
action-cam-add-pattern = Operation Pattern
action-cam-add-pattern-tip = Copy the selected operations' toolpaths in a grid, a circle or a mirror (to cut many copies of a part from one sheet)
action-cam-add-pencil = Pencil (3D)
action-cam-add-pencil-tip = Trace inside corners and valleys one by one to remove what parallel or contour passes left (uses a ball end mill if there is one)
action-cam-add-pin-holes = Pin Holes
action-cam-add-pin-holes-tip = Pin holes to align the stock when flipping it. Added to both the top and bottom setups
action-cam-add-pocket = Pocket
action-cam-add-pocket-tip = Select bottom faces in the 3D view, then press (Shift or Ctrl+click to group several faces). A sketch with closed profiles selected in the timeline works too
action-cam-add-project3d = Project (3D)
action-cam-add-project3d-tip = Drop sketch lines straight down onto the part's faces and trace them. A negative stock to leave cuts below the faces. A selected sketch gives its lines; with nothing selected, the last sketch (uses a ball end mill if there is one)
action-cam-add-radial3d = Radial (3D)
action-cam-add-radial3d-tip = Finish by tracing lines radiating out and in from the part's center (uses a ball end mill if there is one)
action-cam-add-ramp3d = Ramp (3D)
action-cam-add-ramp3d-tip = Finish vertical walls and steep slopes without breaks, going down diagonally 0.5 mm per lap (uses a ball end mill if there is one)
action-cam-add-raster3d = Parallel (3D)
action-cam-add-raster3d-tip = Trace curved faces, slopes and chamfers back and forth in X (uses a ball end mill if there is one)
action-cam-add-rough3d = 3D Roughing
action-cam-add-rough3d-tip = Clear material around a 3D part with offset loops level by level. Leaves 0.3 mm to finish later
action-cam-add-scallop3d = Scallop (3D)
action-cam-add-scallop3d-tip = Finish with loops offset inward at a constant spacing along the surface from the edge of the machining boundary. The cusps stay even on steep areas too. Without a boundary, the part's outline (uses a ball end mill if there is one)
action-cam-add-setup = Setup
action-cam-add-setup-tip = Add a setup to machine the last body
action-cam-add-slot = Slot
action-cam-add-slot-tip = Cut a slot of a set width and depth along the sketch's lines as its center. A selected sketch gives its lines; with nothing selected, the last sketch
action-cam-add-spiral3d = Spiral (3D)
action-cam-add-spiral3d-tip = Finish by tracing a spiral around the part's center from outside in (uses a ball end mill if there is one)
action-cam-add-thread = Thread Milling
action-cam-add-thread-tip = Cut a thread into the selected hole or boss wall with a thread mill. Needs a thread mill in the tool library
action-cam-add-trace = Trace
action-cam-add-trace-tip = Trace the selected model edges or sketch lines, following the line's height. Selected edges are traced with a V-bit; with nothing selected, the sketch's lines
action-cam-add-vcarve = V-Carve
action-cam-add-vcarve-tip = Carve inside closed sketch profiles with a V-bit. Narrow parts are cut shallow to a point, wide parts down to the maximum depth
action-cam-add-waterline = Contour (3D)
action-cam-add-waterline-tip = Go around vertical walls and steep slopes one lap per 0.5 mm of height (uses a ball end mill if there is one)
action-cam-defaults-export = Export Machining Defaults…
action-cam-defaults-export-tip = Write the saved defaults to a JSON file (to take them to another PC)
action-cam-defaults-import = Import Machining Defaults…
action-cam-defaults-import-tip = Read an exported defaults file. Only the kinds in the file are replaced
action-cam-defaults-reset = Reset Machining Defaults
action-cam-defaults-reset-tip = Drop all saved defaults; every operation is added with its initial values
action-cam-export-gcode = Export G-code
action-cam-export-gcode-tip = For Carvera Air. Written next to the document
action-cam-export-gcode-all = Export All Setups as One
action-cam-export-gcode-all-tip = Make one G-code file, with comments between setups prompting to stop and refixture
action-cam-export-gcode-as = Export G-code As…
action-cam-export-gcode-as-tip = Choose where to write it and its name
action-cam-export-gcode-by-tool = Export Sorted by Tool
action-cam-export-gcode-by-tool-tip = Group operations with the same tool to reduce tool changes. When rest machining, manual NC or a cut-out contour would move earlier, it is not sorted and the reason is shown
action-cam-export-gcode-selected = Export Only This Operation
action-cam-export-gcode-selected-tip = Export only the selected operations (to redo just one after a broken tool, for example). CLI and MCP can pick several with operations
action-cam-export-sim-video = Cutting Video…
action-cam-export-sim-video-tip = Make a video of the selected setup being cut from start to finish, from the current view (.mp4, .gif, or numbered .png). Length and size are in the "Scene Settings" of rendering
action-cam-export-stock = Export Cut Stock as STL…
action-cam-export-stock-tip = Save the shape cut by the simulation (at the current time while playing) as STL. A mesh at the grid's resolution
action-cam-fixture-add = Place Fixture
action-cam-fixture-add-tip = Click to place fixtures (clamps). Near threaded holes they snap to the hole. Where they overlap the stock they are moved outside the nearest edge. Toolpaths avoid 2 mm around fixtures
action-cam-holes-ops = Operations from Holes
action-cam-holes-ops-tip = Add spot drilling, pilot drilling, counterbore and countersink chamfer operations together, from the hole features' type, thread and diameter. When the holes change, the toolpaths are regenerated. After changing the type, press again to add missing operations
action-cam-setup-sheet = Export Setup Sheet
action-cam-setup-sheet-tip = Write the stock placement, origin and tool order as Markdown next to the document
action-cam-setup-sheet-html = Export Setup Sheet (HTML)
action-cam-setup-sheet-html-tip = Write an HTML setup sheet next to the document, with feed, depth of cut and length per operation and a top view of the toolpaths. Open it in a browser to print
action-cam-simulate = Simulation
action-cam-simulate-tip = Cut the stock to check for gouges, stock left, and shank and holder collisions. See the shape after each operation on the step bar below
action-cam-simulate-gcode = Check with G-code
action-cam-simulate-gcode-tip = Read back the G-code to be exported and cut with it (exactly what goes to the machine, so post errors are found too)
action-cam-view-gcode = View G-code
action-cam-view-gcode-tip = Check the contents with line numbers before exporting. An estimated time is at the top

## Files

action-io-export-3mf = Export 3MF…
action-io-export-3mf-tip = Make the visible bodies into 3MF for 3D printers. Also writes each body's color (appearance, or material if none), the document's length unit and the design properties (part name, author and so on)
action-io-export-step = Export STEP…
action-io-export-step-tip = Export the last remaining body as STEP
action-io-export-step-each = Export STEP per Body…
action-io-export-step-each-tip = Export each visible body as a separate STEP, named with the body's name after the chosen name
action-io-export-stl = Export STL…
action-io-export-stl-tip = Export the last remaining body as a triangle mesh
action-io-export-stl-each = Export STL per Body…
action-io-export-stl-each-tip = Export each visible body as a separate STL, named with the body's name after the chosen name (part.stl → part-Body1.stl)
action-io-export-view-dxf = Export Current View as DXF…
action-io-export-view-dxf-tip = Make the visible body lines (edges and silhouettes of curved faces) and shown sketch lines from the current viewpoint into a 2D DXF at 1 mm = 1 unit. A perspective view is written as a parallel projection. Hidden lines are not written
action-io-export-view-dxf-hidden = Export Current View as DXF (with Hidden Lines)…
action-io-export-view-dxf-hidden-tip = Add hidden lines to the current view's DXF, as dashed lines on the HIDDEN layer (visible lines on the VISIBLE layer)
action-io-export-view-svg = Export Current View as SVG…
action-io-export-view-svg-tip = Make the visible body lines and shown sketch lines from the current viewpoint into SVG at 1 mm = 1 unit (opens at the same size in laser cutter software such as LightBurn). Lines only, no fill; connected lines are joined into closed outlines. Hidden lines are not written

## Rendering

action-render-animation-video = Animation Video…
action-render-animation-video-tip = Make a video of the step bar (explodes and joint motion) from start to finish. The viewpoint stays as the current view. The file extension picks the format (.mp4, .gif, or numbered .png). Size and frames per second are in "Scene Settings"
action-render-appearance = Appearance
action-render-appearance-tip = Open the window to give bodies, components and faces an appearance (color, metal, roughness). Search the library by category and name, and edit the color and roughness of appearances in this design
action-render-decal-insert = Decal…
action-render-decal-insert-tip = Put an image (PNG, JPEG or BMP, up to 4 MB) on the selected face. The image is stored in the document
action-render-export-gltf = Export glTF…
action-render-export-gltf-tip = Make the visible bodies into glTF (.glb). Also writes the color, metal and roughness of appearances and materials (units in m, Y up)
action-render-light-insert = Light
action-render-light-insert-tip = Place a point light or spotlight above and in front of the bodies. Edit position, target, brightness (lm) and color in the edit panel
action-render-still = Render…
action-render-still-tip = Make a photo-like still image (PNG) of the current view. Ray tracing draws shadows and reflections, then noise is removed. Size and quality are in "Scene Settings"
action-render-turntable = Turntable Video…
action-render-turntable-tip = Make a video going once around the bodies. The file extension picks the format (.mp4, .gif, or numbered .png)

## Simulation

action-study-cancel = Cancel
action-study-cancel-tip = Stop solving (for flow and time-varying heat, the frames so far are kept in the results)
action-study-run = Solve
action-study-run-tip = Solve the selected study. Studies are not solved automatically. Changing conditions or shapes marks the results as "Out of date"

## Commands shown only in the feature right-click menu (timeline, browser, 3D view)
## For commands whose description depends on the feature type (Save as Default, Place Entry Point), the description is written to fit every type.

action-asm-link-break = Break Link
action-asm-link-break-tip = Stop following the source file and keep the current copy (no more notices when the source changes; can be undone)
action-asm-link-pin = Pin This Version
action-asm-link-pin-tip = When pinned, changes to the source file are neither reported nor pulled in
action-asm-link-update = Get Latest
action-asm-link-update-tip = Replace it with the current shape in the source file (can be undone)
action-cad-pattern-axis = Select Axis
action-cad-pattern-axis-tip = Set the axis of the selected pattern (the direction for a rectangular pattern) by clicking an origin X/Y/Z axis, a sketch line or a body edge (a circular edge gives its circle's axis)
action-cad-pattern-axis2 = Select Direction 2
action-cad-pattern-axis2-tip = Set direction 2 of the selected rectangular pattern (the second direction of the grid) by clicking an origin X/Y/Z axis, a sketch line or a body edge (a circular edge gives its circle's axis)
action-cam-contour-chains = Select Contours
action-cam-contour-chains-tip = Click face outlines, hole edges and sketch lines to add or remove them, then press Enter. Any number can be selected. Pressing Enter with none selected uses the part outline
action-cam-contour-tabs = Place Tabs
action-cam-contour-tabs-tip = Click on the toolpath to add or remove tabs, then press Enter. Pressing Enter with none placed spaces them evenly by the tab count field
action-cam-defaults-save = Save Parameters as Default
action-cam-defaults-save-tip = Use this operation's values (cutting conditions, stock to leave, steps and so on) as the starting values for the next operation of the same kind. Faces, tools and setups are not saved
action-cam-entry-place = Place Entry Point
action-cam-entry-place-tip = Start cutting from the clicked point. With a helical entry, the tool spirals down around it
action-cam-floor-add = Add Selected Faces
action-cam-floor-add-tip = Add the flat faces selected in the 3D view to the floor faces (Shift or Ctrl+click selects several)
action-cam-floor-remove = Remove Selected Faces
action-cam-floor-remove-tip = Remove the faces selected in the 3D view from the floor faces
action-cam-rest-pocket = Rest Machining
action-cam-rest-pocket-tip = Cut only the corners and narrow slots this tool could not reach, with the next smaller tool in the library (V and tapered tools too for pockets and contours)
action-cam-setup-add-body = Add Body to Cut
action-cam-setup-add-body-tip = Cut other bodies in the same setup (to cut several parts from one board, for example)
action-cam-setup-origin-pick = Pick Origin in 3D
action-cam-setup-origin-pick-tip = Click a stock box corner, edge midpoint or face center, a point of the part's bounding box, or a part corner to make it the work coordinate origin
action-cam-template-save = Save as Template…
action-cam-template-save-tip = Save the selected operations (all operations inside, for a setup) on this PC under a name to use in another setup or document. Faces and lines are not saved; select them again when using it

## Drawing

action-drawing-add-sheet = Add sheet
action-drawing-add-sheet-tip = Add a sheet to the drawing
action-drawing-base-view = Base view
action-drawing-base-view-tip = Create a base view from the model and a named orientation
action-drawing-projected-view = Projected view
action-drawing-projected-view-tip = Create a projected view from its parent
action-drawing-section-view = Section view
action-drawing-section-view-tip = Create a section from a cutting line in its parent view
action-drawing-detail-view = Detail view
action-drawing-detail-view-tip = Enlarge the region inside a circle in the parent view
action-drawing-move-view = Move view
action-drawing-move-view-tip = Change the paper position or distance from the parent
action-drawing-set-view = Edit view
action-drawing-set-view-tip = Change the scale and visibility of hidden and tangent lines
action-drawing-delete = Delete drawing
action-drawing-delete-tip = Delete a sheet or view; delete child views first
action-drawing-picture = Export drawing lines
action-drawing-picture-tip = Export the sheet geometry and problems as JSON
action-cad-surface-patch = Surface patch
action-cad-surface-patch-tip = Select a closed boundary and press Enter to create a sheet body
action-io-export-obj = Export OBJ…
action-io-export-obj-tip = Export visible bodies as OBJ with object names, vertices, normals and faces. Colors and materials are not written
